  "theory_modules": 3,
  "scope": "For global Lipschitz self-maps u,v of R^m, both actual differentials Du(x) and Dv(u(x)) exist and compose to identity almost everywhere on C={x:v(u(x))=x}. Cover every natural dimension m, retaining the zero-dimensional punctured-approximate-differential convention. Follow Rademacher, null-image transport under v, the chain rule and first-order density uniqueness. Two regressions show the necessary almost-everywhere qualification using the plane axis projection and recover the pointwise conclusion on unit-mass R^0 for arbitrary self-maps.",
